 ### Platform-features run — summary (2026-10-14, night)
 PRs merged (all squash, each bot-reviewed APPROVE with only low findings left): #29 digest flush timer, #31 approval nudge/expiry, #33 replay tests + search attributes, #35 configurable cache TTL (default stays 5m: 1h costs ~16% more at this call spacing), #37 thinking-block round trip + optional adaptive thinking for PR reviews (off: no quality gain on the fixtures, ~9x output tokens at max effort; the model rejects a token budget), #39 structured outputs (native tool search evaluated and not adopted), #41 batch evals. Open: #1 (Langfuse flywheel). Tests 167 -> 219; services run main.
+
+## Reviewer upgrades from pr-sweep — 2026-10-15 (#42)
+- Read the owner's `pr-sweep` skill (a Claude Code skill, so not portable as is) and ported the parts that fit the existing reviewer, with no new tools and no workflow-command changes (replay tests unchanged).
+- **Citation check:** `publish_pr_review` fetches the PR diff and calls `pr_review.check_citations`: a file or line the diff does not show is removed from a finding (the finding is kept, with the original citation moved into its text; the bot review's medium finding was that dropping could lose a real one), the verdict is never changed, and the posted review and the Slack card say how many locations were removed. Any error in the check is swallowed so a review always publishes. Skipped when the head moved, the diff is unavailable (404, 406 too large) or the PR read fails.
+- **Checklist** in the reviewer task (silent test skips, vacuous asserts, over-mocking, tests-only PRs that change prod code, silent reverts; cite only files and lines from the diff).
+- **Per-repo review focus:** `<data_dir>/review-focus/<owner>__<repo>.md`, read in `poll_github`, passed as `pr["review_focus"]`, capped at 3000 chars. Local file only; nothing is read from the PR or the repo.
+- Evals: `review_silent_test_skip` and `review_silent_revert` (soft) pass 3/3, and so do the three existing review cases. Honest note: both new cases also pass 3/3 with the checklist removed, so they are regression guards, not proof the checklist helps.
+- Not ported (decided): model tiering by path, a second verification pass, local pre-push review, stacked-PR handling (the PR dict has no base), and the "any finding means REQUEST_CHANGES" rule (aoa keeps its high-severity rule).
